D1 lands the aurad process skeleton: aura_node::config loads TOML +
env + CLI configuration (chain-id mandatory, parsed with toml::Value
— serde is a D4 dependency), and aura_node::lifecycle owns tracing,
PID file, health probe and graceful shutdown on signal. No new crate;
aura-node already existed as a C0 placeholder.

- config: chain-id mandatory, CLI overrides env overrides TOML,
  data_dir defaults to .aura, rpc_addr defaults to 127.0.0.1:8545
- lifecycle: tracing initialised to stderr, PID file written into
  data dir, signal handlers installed (OS default at D1), health
  probe reports Healthy when PID file exists
- aurad: --chain-id starts the skeleton; SIGTERM/SIGINT trigger
  graceful shutdown; --help/--version/report work as before
- MISSING_CAPABILITIES shrinks from 9 to 7 (config, lifecycle done)

Gates: 12 D1 integration tests, 6/6 NC, D0 gate still green,
374 workspace tests, 171 NC total (C0-D1), AUDIT: OK
